diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8347b4a..c51252b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,27 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and on every pushed
+version tag matching `v*`. It can also be started manually with
+`workflow_dispatch`.
 
 This repository is public.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow authenticates with OIDC and assumes
+`arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in `eu-north-1`. No AWS access
+keys are stored; the `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` secrets
+are no longer used and can be deleted.
+
+The role's trust policy must trust `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` with
+audience `sts.amazonaws.com`, and match `sub` exactly, with no wildcard on the
+repository. Both triggers need an entry, because the subject differs:
+
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/heads/main` for pushes to `main`
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/tags/v*` for version tags (use `StringLike`
+  for this one only)
+
+## Notifications
+
+A Slack message is posted after each deploy through the `SLACK_WEBHOOK`
+secret.
